From: Caboose <caboose@local>
Subject: [PATCH 79/90] Recycle only the sets of pools that never free sets one by one

A reset batched pool kept its sets and handed them out again under their old handles. In a
pool that frees sets individually (ANGLE's, as Chromium Embedded Framework in Halo: MCC uses
it), a late free or use of an old handle then reached the set that now held it, and the
process crashed in descriptor-set allocation or freed an invalid pointer. Such pools give
each allocation a new set; DXVK's pools, which only reset, keep recycling.
---
diff --git a/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan_enc/ResourceTracker.cpp b/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan_enc/ResourceTracker.cpp
--- a/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan_enc/ResourceTracker.cpp
+++ b/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan_enc/ResourceTracker.cpp
@@ -1338,8 +1338,13 @@
 
 void ResourceTracker::clearDescriptorPoolAndUnregisterDescriptorSets(void* context, VkDevice device,
                                                                      VkDescriptorPool pool) {
-    if (cabooseBatchedSets()) {
-        // Caboose: a reset keeps the pool's sets for their ids' next allocation.
+    // Caboose: a reset keeps the pool's sets for their ids' next allocation, in a pool whose
+    // sets are never freed one by one (DXVK's). A pool that frees sets individually gives each
+    // allocation a new set: a kept set reallocated under its old handle would let a late free
+    // or use of that handle (ANGLE's, CEF's) reach the set that now holds it.
+    if (cabooseBatchedSets() &&
+        !(as_goldfish_VkDescriptorPool(pool)->allocInfo->createFlags &
+          VK_DESCRIPTOR_POOL_CREATE_FREE_DESCRIPTOR_SET_BIT)) {
         std::vector<VkDescriptorSetLayout> layouts;
         std::vector<VkDescriptorSet> unrecycled = recycleDescriptorPool(pool, &layouts);
         for (auto setLayout : layouts) decDescriptorSetLayoutRef(context, device, setLayout, nullptr);
